{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogNaStokesHolonomyOrdering","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DilogNaStokesHolonomyOrdering","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.YekutieliIntegration","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesHolonomy.holonomy_growth_order_dependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesHolonomy.holonomy_growth_order_dependent","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesHolonomyOrdering.lean#L109-L126","doc":"**Fibre-level: growth ordering is NOT free.**  There is a (non-abelian) group and two\nsingle-segment paths whose two growth (concatenation) orders give *different*\nholonomies: `holonomy (p ++ q) ≠ holonomy (q ++ p)`.\n\nSo on the non-commutative fibre `𝒫exp` the joint / symmetric limit is **illegal** —\nit would scramble the path-ordering of the holonomy — whereas the abelian τ-shadow is\norder-free (`partBHolonomy_reorder_free`).  This is the structural reason the na-Stokes\npath-ordering **selects the iterated (not joint) limit** for Part B: the two limits are\ninterchangeable only in the abelian degeneration, and the physical observable is a\npath-ordered holonomy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesHolonomy.partBHolonomy_reorder_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesHolonomy.partBHolonomy_reorder_free","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesHolonomyOrdering.lean#L99-L107","doc":"**τ-shadow ordering-freedom (abelian collapse).**  Reordering the segments leaves the\nscalar Part-B holonomy unchanged — the classical (abelian) limit of Yekutieli's\nnon-abelian Stokes, where the surface-ordering is irrelevant (`holonomy_perm`).  So in\nthe commutative τ-shadow the *value* of the multiplicative integral is independent of\nthe refinement order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesHolonomy.partBHolonomy_eq_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesHolonomy.partBHolonomy_eq_prod","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesHolonomyOrdering.lean#L85-L97","doc":"**Φ_n IS an ordered holonomy.**  The Part-B partial product `∏_{k<n}(1 − x qᵏ)⁻¹`\nequals the discrete holonomy (ordered product) of its scalar segment transports.\nThe τ-shadow identification half of qou-zbcj — the recognisable observable *is* an\nordered product of segment transports. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesHolonomy.partBHolonomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesHolonomy.partBHolonomy","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesHolonomyOrdering.lean#L80-L83","doc":"The Part-B partial product `Φ_n` presented as a **discrete Yekutieli holonomy**: the\nordered `List.prod` of the first `n` scalar segment transports, in path order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesHolonomy.partBSeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesHolonomy.partBSeg","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesHolonomyOrdering.lean#L76-L78","doc":"The `k`-th Part-B scalar segment transport, `(1 − x qᵏ)⁻¹` — the τ-shadow of the\n`k`-th local parallel transport of the path-ordered holonomy. ","signatureChunk":0}]}